"q-130313" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293659 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cbbffd2-c482-515d-8bcc-7e95b417ee3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cbbffd2-c482-515d-8bcc-7e95b417ee3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293661} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc6da346-ec1e-523a-acd9-74dfb0bb9e66" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293660} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid 